.TH ASTERCTL-BLOB-STATUS 1 "2026-10-20" "Aster" "User Commands"
.\" <!-- ASTER-BLOB-CAPABILITY:BEGIN -->
.\" ```json
.\" {
.\"   "schema": 1,
.\"   "surface": "blob_status_man",
.\"   "blob_status_scope": "receiver_local_durable_state",
.\"   "blob_status_reports_remote_delivery_peer_or_convergence": false
.\" }
.\" ```
.\" <!-- ASTER-BLOB-CAPABILITY:RENDERED -->
.\" blob-status reports receiver-local durable state, not remote delivery, peer status, or convergence.
.\" <!-- ASTER-BLOB-CAPABILITY:END -->
.SH NAME
asterctl-blob-status \- inspect or wait for receiver-local Blob publication state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B blob-status
.BI \-\-publication-id " ID"
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
.RI [ \-\-wait ]
.RI [ \-\-poll-ms " N" ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asterctl blob-status
reports exact durable state held by the local Aster node for one authenticated
profile-5 Blob publication identity and exact topic/scope selector.
.PP
Local publication is peer-independent. Waiting for
.B available
observes one node's canonical publication state; it neither starts contact nor
confirms that any other node has converged.
.PP
Snapshot mode performs one request and exits successfully for every valid
state, including
.BR missing .
The
.B missing
state intentionally covers both an absent publication and one the caller is
not currently authorized to inspect.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-wait ,
the command keeps at most one request in flight and polls until
.BR available ,
.BR expired-or-retired ,
or the global client deadline. The latter two outcomes exit unsuccessfully and
print the final complete snapshot. Local publication and durable storage do not
depend on this polling command or on destination availability.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-publication-id " ID"
Required publication ID from
.BR asterctl-blob-publish (1),
as Base64-encoded 32 bytes. This is distinct from the finalized Blob ID.
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
Required exact Blob topic.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Required exact Blob scope.
.TP
.B \-\-wait
Poll until an available or terminal state, bounded by the global
.B \-\-timeout
deadline.
.TP
.BI \-\-poll-ms " N"
Polling interval from 100 through 60000 milliseconds. Default: 1000.
Requires
.BR \-\-wait .
.SH STATES
.TP
.B missing
No currently visible durable evidence. This is not an existence oracle.
.TP
.B awaiting-data
The publication is admitted and awaits its first durable data unit.
.TP
.B receiving
Durable plaintext and authenticated-transfer counters are advancing.
.TP
.B ready-to-finalize
All publication units are durable and finalization remains.
.TP
.B available
Finalization completed; the response includes the content-addressed Blob ID.
.TP
.B expired-or-retired
The publication cannot continue under retained lifecycle evidence.
.SH OUTPUT
Text and JSON distinguish plaintext bytes from authenticated transfer bytes.
The counters and states are receiver-local durable facts and contain no
inference about a remote node or the IP, non-IP, BLE, or future transport used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Snapshot returned a valid state, or wait reached
.BR available .
.TP
.B 1
RPC or validation failed, the deadline elapsed, or wait reached
.BR expired-or-retired .
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-blob-publish (1),
.BR asterctl-blob-read (1)
